(docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #115 - the `value`-variable landing site: #114 only
 cast a map-value read, so a `value` local's runtime-tagged payload was
 still copied as raw bits into a mismatched destination. Reading a
 `value` into a `text` used to SIGSEGV on first print; the general fix
 casts it exactly as `v as a text` would.)

a value called v is 42.
a text called t is v.
Print "{t}".
